Map BEC tactics to MITRE ATT&CK techniques in an O365 environment:

```python
# BEC MITRE ATT&CK mapping for O365
bec_mitre_mapping = {
    'Initial Access': {
        'T1566.001': 'Spearphishing Attachment',
        'T1566.002': 'Spearphishing Link',
        'T1078': 'Valid Accounts (compromised credentials)'
    },
    'Persistence': {
        'T1098': 'Account Manipulation (inbox rules, forwarding)',
        'T1114': 'Email Collection (reading sensitive emails)'
    },
    'Defense Evasion': {
        'T1070': 'Indicator Removal (deleting sent/deleted items)',
        'T1562': 'Impair Defenses (disabling MFA)'
    },
    'Collection': {
        'T1114.001': 'Local Email Collection',
        'T1114.002': 'Remote Email Collection'
    },
    'Command and Control': {
        'T1071.001': 'Web Protocols (O365 API abuse)'
    }
}

# Print the attack chain
for tactic, techniques in bec_mitre_mapping.items():
    print(f'\n{tactic}:')
    for tid, tname in techniques.items():
        print(f'  {tid} - {tname}')
```

This mapping helps you correlate detections and build investigation timelines.
